# No *tracking state* listed here, by design — and NOT because none can appear.
#
# The tracking skills keep local state under <base>/.claude/, where <base> is the
# directory Claude was invoked in. Run one with this repo as the base and you get:
#   .claude/.tracking/<org>/       the tracking clone
#   .claude/<org>.status.json      session cursor
#   .claude/<org>.snapshot.json    report cursor
#   .claude/snapshots/             /snapshot's local report copies
#   .claude/tracking-org           the org login, when nothing else answers
#
# Those are kept out of `git status` by <toplevel>/.git/info/exclude, which the
# skills write themselves — NOT by this file. That is the whole point: .gitignore
# is tracked, so listing them here would be a skill modifying a product repo's
# contents and landing in someone's commit. .git/info/exclude is local and
# untracked, so the exclusion costs the repo nothing.
#
# Nothing lives at ~/.claude/ — that is Claude Code's own config directory.
# .claude/skills/ is ordinary tracked source and none of the above applies to it.
# See docs/target-workflow.md §2.

# OS cruft, which is not state and has no business here either. (msa1624/skills#38)
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
